+# @deepseek-ai/dsh-goal-progress-guard
+
+Advisory goal-round progress guard for the same-session goal loop.
+
+The goal-round driver continues an armed goal purely on `phase === 'active'`,
+so a model can idle through its round budget without changing anything. This
+plugin closes that gap from the outside: it classifies every admitted goal
+round's tool trail from the session event log and acts at the next round's
+admission.
+
+## Behavior
+
+Per admitted goal round (a `user/message` with a positive goal `round`), the
+guard pairs `tool/call` with `tool/result` and classifies the round at
+`turn/end`:
+
+- **progress** — at least one successful result from a `mutationTools` pattern.
+- **observation** — no mutation, but at least one successful result (reads,
+  searches, subagent spawns). Counted as progress-adjacent: the streak resets.
+- **noop** — zero tool calls, or every call failed. The consecutive
+  no-progress streak increments.
+
+Before the next round of the same goal enters its step, a live streak either:
+
+- **advisory (default)** — appends a logged `<goal_progress>` notice to the
+  admitted messages naming the last round's counters and the streak, telling
+  the model to change strategy or report blocked. Logged implies
+  model-visible, so the notice survives replay.
+- **blocking (`blockAfterNoProgressRounds > 0`)** — once the streak reaches
+  the threshold, the guard blocks the goal through `goals.block` with code
+  `no-progress` and rejects the round; the driver fails closed because the
+  goal phase is no longer `active`.
+
+The handler delegates before acting and never touches the driver's
+reservation bookkeeping, so it composes with `dsh-goal-round-driver` in
+either waterfall order. A round rejected by the guard converges through the
+driver's stale-attempt path.
+
+## Configuration
+
+| Field | Default | Meaning |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `mutationTools` | `['write', 'edit', 'apply_patch', 'str_replace*']` | `*`-wildcard tool-name patterns whose successful result counts as a verifiable state mutation. |
+| `blockAfterNoProgressRounds` | `0` | Hard-block the goal after this many consecutive no-progress rounds; `0` keeps the guard advisory-only. |
+
+Misconfiguration (empty patterns, negative or non-integer threshold) throws at
+plugin load. The plugin is not part of shipped default profiles; opt in
+through a profile overlay:
+
+```yaml
+plugins:
+  - id: goal-progress-guard
+    name: '@deepseek-ai/dsh-goal-progress-guard'
+    config:
+      blockAfterNoProgressRounds: 3
+```
+
+## Model Experience
+
+The guard adds one user-role `<goal_progress>` notice (bounded, well under
+100 tokens) to a goal round's admitted messages, only while a no-progress
+streak is live. It neither compacts nor rewrites history; token and KV-cache
+effects are those of one extra short notice per flagged round.
+
+## Known Limitations and Deferred Work
+
+- Signal vocabulary is heuristic: a round that only reads files counts as
+  `observation` even when the read was redundant. Sharper signals (test
+  red→green transitions, diff hashes) are deferred to a follow-up that prices
+  them from `tool/result.meta`.
+- A round spent waiting on delegated subagents counts as `observation` (the
+  spawn call succeeded), so the streak does not fire during normal
+  delegation; a deployment whose subagent tool returns synchronously should
+  add that tool to `mutationTools` or accept advisory notices.
+- The block path converts an admitted `enter` decision into `reject` after
+  downstream listeners ran; the driver converges via its stale-attempt
+  handling, but a dedicated pre-reserve seam in the driver would be cleaner
+  and is the intended upstream follow-up.
+- This package omits `./invariant`: its only cross-component relation (notice
+  precedes the round that follows a no-op) is asserted directly by the
+  behavior suite, and there is no second independent observation to diverge.
